A `prefix.changed` naming a request that carries no `head_sha256`. A change is
a difference between two digests, and this row names a request that has none.

The record is `adapted`, which is the one source under which a request may go
unhashed: a foreign harness's log records what was said, not the bytes that
were sent. An adapter with no head to hash has no head change to report either,
and this refusal is what stops it reporting one anyway.
